# koblas

Kotlin Multiplatform BLAS and LAPACK.

## Verify

- Run `./gradlew :koblas:check :koblas-bench:check lintDocs`. Bare `./gradlew check` also rebuilds the native libs in `koblas-openblas`/`koblas-suitesparse`/`koblas-basiclu`/`koblas-hfactor` from source; reserve it for touching those modules or before pushing.
- Default tests use the reference backend. Use `-Pkoblas.hostTests=true` for OpenBLAS/SuiteSparse and additionally `-Pkoblas.noSimd=true` for scalar thresholds, level-2 bindings, and small-size dispatch.

## Tests

- Match existing framework, layout, fixtures, and assertion style; arrange → act → assert.
- Name classes `<FileUnderTest>Test`; use ASCII backtick test names with words only—no `()`, `#`, or commas.
- Test one observable behavior, parameterize variants, and keep JVM tests under 300 ms.
- Compare backends with the portable reference via `assert*AgreesWithReference`, not hand values.
- `wellConditioned` has identity pivots; perturb it before testing pivoting or row permutations.

## Design

- Public concrete containers use the intentional unprefixed names (`DenseMatrix`, `SparseMatrix`, `DenseVector`,
  `SparseVector`); do not restore `F64` aliases. A future element family needs an explicit API and seam design.
- Dense matrices are column-major: `A(i, j)` is `i + j * rows`. Sparse matrices are validated CSC with ascending row indices per column.
- The portable reference defines semantics. Host bindings use measured thresholds then fall back to it.
- Backend seams retain the strongest per half; equal offers preserve first registration. Registration is CAS; call `installBackends` at startup.
- `*Into` destinations may alias inputs; test the backing buffer.
- A helper returning a `DoubleVector` must be `inline`. A vector returned from a call the JIT declines to inline becomes a heap object, so the loop allocates per operation and runs twenty to forty times slower, silently and only sometimes: the refusal depends on how close the whole compilation sits to its node budget, so a caller's size decides it. Suppress `NOTHING_TO_INLINE` and say why.

## Style and contributions

- Prefer clear names/types. Comments explain why, never narrate changes or cite issues; retain `TODO`/`FIXME`.
- Public APIs get KDoc. Write math as `A(i, j)` and use `[Symbol]` links.
- Do not edit `.github/` unless asked. Read `koblas-bench/README.md` before benchmarks; cite KDoc performance figures only from its suites.
- Commits are single-line conventional commits without scopes, bodies, or trailers (for example `fix: handle empty input`). PR bodies follow `.github/pull_request_template.md` with `Closes #NN` first.
